      "message": "I tried, this is what I got down to:\n\n$(shell \\\n  stage_file\u003d$$(printf \u0027%s\u0027 $(env_config).$$$$); \\\n  [ -d $(out) ] || mkdir -p $(out); \\\n  for env_flag in $(ENV_VARS); do \\\n    printf \"/* %s\u003d%s */\\n\" $${env_flag} $${$${env_flag}} \u003e\u003e $${stage_file}; \\\n  done; \\\n  cmp -s $${stage_file} $${env_config} \u0026\u0026 rm -f $${stage_file} || \\\n    mv $${stage_file} $${env_config})\n\n\nthere is a problem with this line though:\n\nprintf \"/* %s\u003d%s */\\n\" $${env_flag} $${$${env_flag}} \u003e\u003e $${stage_file};\n\nsince env_flag is not a make variable any more, its expansion is not working, and since default make shell is sh, as opposed to bash, indirection ${!var_name} is not working either.\n\nOn top of that the original code is shorter, because it is using more succinct foreach() instead of for(); do : done and does not need so many end of line escapes.",
